    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="42.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 42.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="76" ed="#liebermann"/>Eac we cweðað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.15"/>, þæt mon mote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.16"/> mid his hlaforde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.17"/> feohtan orwige, gif mon on ðone hlaford<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.18"/> fiohte; swa mót se hlaford mid þy men feohtan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.5" corresp="#wit-ot-frags"><pb n="76" ed="#liebermann"/>... cwæðað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon ...aford ...wige, gif mon...</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="42.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="76" ed="#liebermann"/>Eac we cweðaþ, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.3"/> mote mid his hlaforde feohtan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.13"/> orwige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.14"/>, gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.3"/> on þone hlaford fiohte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.15-2"/>; swa mot se hlaford mid þa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.16-2"/></hi> men feohtan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="42.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="77" ed="#liebermann"/>Item diximus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.10"/>, ut homini liceat pugnare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.11-2"/> cum domino suo sine wita, si quis assalliat ipsum dominum. Sic liceat domino pugnare cum homine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.oe.12"/> suo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="84" ed="#attenborough"/>Eac we cweðað, þæt mon mote mid his hlaforde feohtan orwige<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_42-5.attnote.fn.14"/>, gif mon on ðone hlaford fiohte; swa mót se hlaford mid þy<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Af_42-5.attnote.fn.15"/> men feohtan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="45" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="344" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Eac we cweðað, þæt mon mote mid his hlaforde feohtan orwige, gif mon on ðone hlaford fiohte; swa mót se hlaford mid þy men feohtan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="77" ed="#liebermann"/>Auch bestimmen wir, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.de.1"/> man bei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.de.2"/> seinem Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.de.3"/> fechten darf, ohne Fehde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.de.4"/> [auf sich zu laden], vorausgesetzt, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_42-5.lnote.de.5"/> jemand gegen diesen Herrn ficht; ebenso darf der Herr bei dem Manne fechten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">We also determine that one may fight on behalf of one’s lord without [incurring] feud, provided that someone is fighting against that lord; likewise the lord may fight on behalf of his man.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="85" ed="#attenborough"/>We further declare that a man may fight on behalf of his lord, if his lord is attacked, without becoming liable to vendetta<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_42-5.attnote.n.1"/>. Under similar conditions a lord may fight on behalf of his man.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="416" ed="#whitelock"/>Moreover we declare that a man may fight on behalf of his lord, if the lord is being attacked, without incurring a vendetta. Similarly the lord may fight on behalf of his man.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="345" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Likewise we declare, that one may fight at the side of his lord without incurring liability if someone fights against his lord; the lord may similarly fight at the side of [his] man.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="271"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-49-7">Af El 49.7</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cwædaþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cwædaþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mot <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mot Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rd feahtan <hi rend="spaced">orwite</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rd feahtan <hi rend="italic">orwite</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rde feahte <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rde feahte Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">und</hi> a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e and a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> on wige</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to on wige</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> feohte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to feohte</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ā <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ā on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dux. <hi rend="italic">Or;</hi> Interdix. <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> I. d. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dux. Or; Interdix. instead of I. d. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inpu. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inpu. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">domino <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">domino Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt in Hn 82, 3. 88, 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used in Hn 82, 3. 88, 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in Beihilfe für</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in support of</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gefolge 15c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gefolge 15c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der nur hier und 42, 7 begegnende Sinn ward seit 11. Jh. nicht mehr verstanden. Sonst bed. <hi rend="italic">orwige: imbellis</hi> ‘kampfunfähig’; Toller. Den hier erforderten passivischen Sinn gewährt, aber aus ‘Fehde’ gebildet, mhd. <hi rend="italic">urvech</hi> ‘unangefochten’. — H ändert ‘im Kampfe [des Herrn]’; ‘ohne Strafgeld’ = <hi rend="italic">forisfacto</hi> 42, 7 Ld Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The sense, found only here and in 42, 7, was no longer understood from the 11th cent. onwards. Elsewhere <hi rend="italic">orwige</hi> means <hi rend="italic">imbellis</hi>, ‘unfit for fighting’; Toller. The passive sense required here is provided, though formed from ‘feud’, by Middle High German <hi rend="italic">urvech</hi> ‘unchallenged’. — H alters to ‘in the fight [of the lord]’; ‘without fine’ = <hi rend="italic">forisfacto</hi> 42, 7 Ld Q</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_42-5.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Des Herrn Kampf muss also Notwehr sein; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4a. 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The lord’s fighting must therefore be in self-defence; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4a. 9</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-5.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>orwige</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Altered to <hi rend="italic">on wige</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">orwite</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_42-5.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">84</biblScope></bibl><label>þy</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þam</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_42-5.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The word <hi rend="italic">orwige</hi> here evidently denotes a man who, having committed homicide (under the circumstances specified), is protected from vengeance at the hands of the relatives of the man he has slain. In later times the meaning of <hi rend="italic">orwige</hi> was not understood—hence <hi rend="italic">on wige</hi> (‘in fight’) in H, and <hi rend="italic">sine wita</hi> (‘without fine’) in Quadr.</seg></note>
      </div>
